WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.415
Marcus breaks his wrist on March 1.

00:00:02.415 --> 00:00:06.555
The notice of claim provision requires him to tell the insurer within

00:00:06.555 --> 00:00:10.350
20 days of the loss, or as soon as reasonably possible.

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:14.835
Notice can be a phone call or a letter to the insurer or

00:00:14.835 --> 00:00:19.320
its authorized producer, and it need only identify the insured and the policy.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:22.080
Late notice does not defeat the claim if

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:24.840
it was given as soon as reasonably possible.

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:29.670
For disability income policies that pay for a long period, the insured may be

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:34.500
required to give proof of continuing disability at reasonable intervals, usually every six months.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:38.017
Once the insurer receives notice, it must send Marcus the forms

00:00:38.017 --> 00:00:41.215
it wants used for proof of loss within 15 days.

00:00:41.215 --> 00:00:44.733
If the forms do not arrive in that time, Marcus may

00:00:44.733 --> 00:00:48.250
submit proof in any written form describing the occurrence, character and

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:51.448
extent of the loss, and the insurer must accept it.

00:00:51.448 --> 00:00:55.285
The provision prevents an insurer from stalling a claim by withholding paperwork.

00:00:55.285 --> 00:00:58.802
In practice the clock runs from the insurer’s receipt of notice,

00:00:58.802 --> 00:01:02.000
and producers often help clients by supplying the forms directly.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:06.199
Written proof of loss must be furnished within 90 days after the loss.

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:10.074
For a continuing loss such as disability, the 90 days run from

00:01:10.074 --> 00:01:13.627
the end of each period for which the insurer is liable.

00:01:13.627 --> 00:01:17.503
If it was not reasonably possible to meet the deadline, proof is

00:01:17.503 --> 00:01:21.378
accepted as soon as reasonably possible, but no later than one year

00:01:21.378 --> 00:01:24.608
after it was due, unless the claimant was legally incapacitated.

00:01:24.608 --> 00:01:27.192
Proof of loss is the medical and financial

00:01:27.192 --> 00:01:29.775
documentation that lets the insurer decide the claim.

00:01:29.775 --> 00:01:32.359
It is different from notice, which merely alerts

00:01:32.359 --> 00:01:34.620
the insurer that a claim is coming.

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:38.492
After receiving proof, the insurer must pay claims immediately, which Maryland’s

00:01:38.492 --> 00:01:42.364
prompt payment law defines as within 30 days for clean claims,

00:01:42.364 --> 00:01:46.237
with interest at 1.5 percent a month starting on day 31.

00:01:46.237 --> 00:01:49.053
Benefits for a continuing loss, such as disability

00:01:49.053 --> 00:01:51.517
income, must be paid at least monthly.

00:01:51.517 --> 00:01:56.093
Death benefits go to the named beneficiary or, if none, to the estate.

00:01:56.093 --> 00:01:59.965
All other benefits go to the insured, or at the insured’s

00:01:59.965 --> 00:02:03.838
direction to the hospital or physician under an assignment of benefits.

00:02:03.838 --> 00:02:08.414
A facility of payment clause lets the insurer pay up to a small

00:02:08.414 --> 00:02:12.990
amount, often 1,000 dollars, to a relative who is caring for the insured.

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:17.459
The insurer may have the insured examined by a physician of its choosing, at

00:02:17.459 --> 00:02:21.609
its own expense, as often as reasonably necessary while a claim is pending.

00:02:21.609 --> 00:02:24.163
In case of death it may require an

00:02:24.163 --> 00:02:26.717
autopsy where the law does not forbid one.

00:02:26.717 --> 00:02:30.867
The legal actions provision sets the window for suing the insurer: no suit

00:02:30.867 --> 00:02:35.016
may be filed until 60 days after proof of loss has been given,

00:02:35.016 --> 00:02:39.166
which gives the insurer time to pay, and no suit may be filed

00:02:39.166 --> 00:02:42.359
more than three years after proof of loss was required.

00:02:42.359 --> 00:02:45.870
Inside that window the insured keeps full access to the courts.

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:49.811
Where a policy pays a death benefit, such as AD and D,

00:02:49.811 --> 00:02:53.751
the insured may change the beneficiary at any time unless the designation

00:02:53.751 --> 00:02:57.692
was made irrevocable; the consent of a revocable beneficiary is not needed.

00:02:57.692 --> 00:03:00.976
Maryland also lists cancellation by the insured among the provisions

00:03:00.976 --> 00:03:04.259
to know: an insured may cancel an individual policy by

00:03:04.259 --> 00:03:07.215
written notice, and the insurer returns the unearned premium.

00:03:07.215 --> 00:03:11.484
Put the clocks together for Marcus: notice within 20 days, forms within 15,

00:03:11.484 --> 00:03:15.753
proof within 90, payment within 30, suit between 60 days and three years.

00:03:15.753 --> 00:03:18.380
Say them in order until they are automatic.
